// agent-emission.proto — THE agent-output vocabulary.
//
// One closed oneof naming everything an agent can produce inside a
// conversation. It is deliberately NOT a feed message: it carries no uuid, no
// timestamp, no ordering and no provenance, because it is used in two places
// that stamp those differently —
//
//   1. the top-level feed, where ConversationItem (feed.proto) wraps it with
//      the session's own identity/ordering/provenance stamps, and
//   2. a detached agent's bubble, where AsyncAgentUpdate (async-bubble.proto)
//      wraps it with a bubble id and that bubble's fold accounting.
//
// The same message serves both because a detached agent is not a second,
// weaker kind of conversation — it is the same conversation happening
// somewhere else. A renderer written for the main feed therefore renders a
// detached agent unchanged.
